    {
      "id": "CARD-AM-10-concept",
      "conceptId": "C-AM-10",
      "kind": "concept",
      "title": {
        "en": "Phase modulation and FM–PM distinction",
        "or": "Phase modulation ଓ FM–PM ତଫାତ"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Phase modulation, or PM, changes the instantaneous phase of a constant-amplitude carrier directly according to the message. Its form is s(t)=Ac*cos(2*pi*fc*t+kp*m(t)), where kp is phase sensitivity. FM and PM are both angle modulation, but their direct message relationships differ: FM frequency deviation follows the message, while PM phase deviation follows the message. Because instantaneous frequency is the rate of change of phase divided by 2*pi, PM frequency deviation follows the derivative of the message. A constant message produces a fixed phase shift in PM rather than a sustained frequency offset. PM completes our chapter comparison and is not a prerequisite for the selected lab.",
        "or": "Phase modulation କିମ୍ବା PM ରେ Message ଅନୁସାରେ constant-amplitude Carrier ର instantaneous Phase ସିଧାସଳଖ ବଦଳେ। s(t)=Ac*cos(2*pi*fc*t+kp*m(t)), ଯେଉଁଠି kp ହେଉଛି Phase sensitivity। FM ଓ PM ଦୁଇଟି Angle modulation। FM ର Frequency deviation Message ଅନୁସାରେ, PM ର Phase deviation Message ଅନୁସାରେ ବଦଳେ। Instantaneous Frequency ହେଉଛି Phase ର rate of change କୁ 2*pi ଦ୍ୱାରା ଭାଗ କଲେ ମିଳୁଥିବା ମୂଲ୍ୟ। ତେଣୁ PM ର Frequency deviation Message ର derivative ଅନୁସାରେ ବଦଳେ। Constant message PM ରେ fixed Phase shift ଦିଏ। PM ଏହି lab ର ପୂର୍ବଶର୍ତ୍ତ ନୁହେଁ।"
      },
